{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482384-does-anyone-write-transcripts-for-their-games","id":1482384,"title":"Does anyone write Transcripts for their games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-30T10:21:49-07:00","id":1482384,"title":"Does anyone write Transcripts for their games?","content":"I'm midway through <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/27416067-dialogue\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Dialogue</i></a>, by Robert McKee. Someone at a writing group who works in the industry advised me to do a screenplay, an idea that got shelved due to more immediate concerns and obligations. In my Mage campaign, there are two upcoming adventures where a conversation between NPCs are important for the players to be able to understand in detail. One is a meeting between mages that is perfectly recalled by an attendee with Mind 1+. The other is an interrogation of a prisoner that was audio recorded and then typed. <br /> <br /> Typing transcripts might be overdoing session-prep. On the other hand, I think giving players something really substantial to mull over while in character would reduce the need for me to answer player questions and allow me to observe how they approach specific problem solving. I get to think about the next session while they are focused on the previously written content. <br /> <br /> Do you write transcripts for your games or would you consider it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T09:14:09-07:00","id":1483041,"title":"","content":"I tried writing diary reports from some of my characters viewpoints after a game. It's makes for a fun creative experience and helps flesh your player's personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T10:13:35-07:00","id":1483048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482384-does-anyone-write-transcripts-for-their-games?p=1483041#post1483041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried writing diary reports from some of my characters viewpoints after a game. It's makes for a fun creative experience and helps flesh your player's personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it easier to focus on one character who is more active in a conversation, because it easier to makes their voice distinct. In writing, that consists of expressions they use, average length of sentences, which subjects they elaborate most on and other flavors.<br /> <br /> If I were doing a diary, I would do the same as in my current chronicle and make the character <i>dead</i>. This limits the scope of the writing and creates a situation, if the character was sufficiently important, where other people can express views on the person and their activities before death. One character might say, &quot;He was a rotten bastard.&quot;. Another, speaking more slowly, might say, &quot;If only he hadn't given in to his vices, we would all have benefited from what he was trying to create. There won't be another like him, I'm afraid.&quot;. The circumstance of the character being dead lets you convey a lot about pre-existing relationships in short blurbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T21:07:39-07:00","id":1516311,"title":"","content":"I really look forward to this game can develop further. <div align=\"right\"><a href=\"https://slope-game.io\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">slope game</span></span></a></div> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27906-toyotasolid","name":"toyotasolid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T03:07:21-07:00","id":1523127,"title":"","content":"that's awesome information, thanks a lot! Many students often wonder, &quot;<a href=\"https://www.geekandnerd.org/papersowl-com-review/\" target=\"_blank\">is papersowl legit\u200b</a>?&quot; Based on my research and personal experience, I can confirm that PapersOwl is a legitimate academic writing service. They provide assistance with various types of assignments, and their writers deliver papers that meet academic standards.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27332-neelyang77","user":"neelyang77","date":". 10-01-2023, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27332-neelyang77","name":"neelyang77","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T10:51:39-07:00","id":1523221,"title":"","content":"I have been writing transcripts largely now from a single character's point of view that I have gelled well with on a playing basis. It's quite a amazing feeling when you have one of moments of creative outputs where everything seems to click into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T10:04:14-07:00","id":1523917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482384-does-anyone-write-transcripts-for-their-games#post1482384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm midway through <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/27416067-dialogue\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Dialogue</i></a>, by Robert McKee. Someone at a writing group who works in the industry advised me to do a screenplay, an idea that got shelved due to more immediate concerns and obligations. In my Mage campaign, there are two upcoming adventures where a conversation between NPCs are important for the players to be able to understand in detail. One is a meeting between mages that is perfectly recalled by an attendee with Mind 1+. The other is an interrogation of a prisoner that was audio recorded and then typed.<br /> <br /> Typing transcripts might be overdoing session-prep. On the other hand, I think giving players something really substantial to mull over while in character would reduce the need for me to answer player questions and allow me to observe how they approach specific problem solving. I get to think about the next session while they are focused on the previously written content.<br /> If you've ever wondered about the <a href=\"https://gamblorium.com/uk/blog/best-roulette-strategies/\" target=\"_blank\">best way to win at roulette\u200b</a>, I have a story to share. It's not about a guaranteed method, but rather a strategy that worked for me. I've found that focusing on even-money bets like red or black, even or odd, and 1-18 or 19-36 offers a more balanced approach. This strategy reduces risk and prolongs gameplay. Pair it with setting limits for wins and losses, and you'll find yourself in a more controlled and enjoyable gambling experience. Remember, roulette is a game of chance, and there are no surefire ways to win, but this approach has certainly improved my odds and made it all the more exciting.<br /> <br /> Do you write transcripts for your games or would you consider it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it can be great experience to test it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","user":"Dazert1","date":". 10-20-2023, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","name":"Dazert1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27939_1.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T07:36:39-07:00","id":1524136,"title":"","content":"I practice speed typing as a hobby. In the future, I'm planning to learn stenography, which is the same system that court recorders use to take super accurate real time transcripts of court proceedings, but for now all I use is just a keyboard (an expensive one that has contactless switches that I really like, but it's just a regular keyboard nonetheless).<br /> <br /> At this moment I don't get input rates fast enough to quite fast enough to transcribe in real time, but sometimes I actually enjoy sitting in on other people's games (with everyone onboard with it, of course) and practicing speed typing by seeing how long and how thoroughly I can keep up with their game. Depending on how fast the players and GM speak and how back-and-forth the banter is I might be able to get it word for word, other times, I might just have to resort to summing stuff up, but afterwards the GM and players should have a pretty accurate record of how the session went, which works great for them because it gives them something of an &quot;Actual Play&quot; that they can use for their own use. I rather like it because it's often more engaging and feels more lifelike and it's more candid than trying to simply transcribe a recording.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jester-PFG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27707_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T12:01:20-07:00","id":1524433,"title":"","content":"I do not, but maybe I should.<br /> <br /> It sounds interesting now that I think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T10:30:14-08:00","id":1525260,"title":"","content":"It does help Matt Corleone for just as creative excerise and flesh out your favorite characters more and more 3 dimensional to yourself and others who might read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}